 "result": "csvsum.py is a flat-token version: it reads all of stdin as bytes, turns newlines into commas, splits on commas, and sums val by cat using slices t[4::3] and t[5::3] (header skipped). It writes the sorted 'cat,sum' lines with 2 decimals. It matched the sample out-0.txt byte for byte. Its variant was adopted in the bench at +7% over the baseline of 2.02383, and the kit's noise is 4.8%. I'm resting here because that gain is banked and I have no tested idea that clearly beats it.",
